---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Parts Relay brand guidelines | Parts Relay"
  description="Get the official Parts Relay artwork, logo files, type specifications and colour values for print and digital use."
>
  <div class="brand">
    <aside class="brand-side">
      <div class="brand-side-inner">
        <img class="brand-symbol" src="/assets/symbol.svg" alt="Parts Relay symbol" />
        <nav aria-label="Brand guidelines">
          <button type="button" data-jump="brand-intro">
            Introduction
          </button>
          <button type="button" data-jump="brand-marks">
            Logo &amp; symbol
          </button>
          <button type="button" data-jump="brand-placement">
            Placement
          </button>
          <button type="button" data-jump="brand-colors">
            Color
          </button>
          <button type="button" data-jump="brand-type">
            Typography
          </button>
          <button type="button" data-jump="brand-files">
            Download files
          </button>
        </nav>
        <a
          href="/assets/parts-relay-brand-kit.zip"
          download="Parts-Relay-Brand-Kit.zip"
          class="brand-download"
        >
          Download brand assets ↓
        </a>
      </div>
    </aside>
    <div class="brand-main">
      <header class="brand-hero" id="brand-intro">
        <div class="brand-hero-copy">
          <h1 tabindex="-1">
            Parts Relay
            <br />
            brand guidelines
          </h1>
          <p>
            Download the official Parts Relay logos, colors and type specifications for your
            publication, presentation or website.
          </p>
        </div>
        <img
          class="brand-rotor"
          src="/assets/rotor-print.svg"
          alt="A brake disc illustrated in a halftone pattern"
        />
      </header>
      <p class="brand-lede">
        The two dots in the symbol stand for the shop and the parts counter. The line between them
        follows a request.
      </p>
      <section class="brand-chapter" id="brand-marks" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>Logo &amp; symbol</h2>
        <p>
          Choose the wordmark for a full signature. The symbol works on its own in a small control
          or app tile.
        </p>
        <div class="brand-assets">
          <div class="brand-asset">
            <div class="brand-preview">
              <img src="/assets/logo.svg" alt="Parts Relay horizontal logo" />
            </div>
            <a download="parts-relay-logo.svg" href="/assets/logo.svg">
              Primary wordmark <span>SVG ↓</span>
            </a>
          </div>
          <div class="brand-asset">
            <div class="brand-preview brand-dark">
              <img src="/assets/logo-white.svg" alt="Parts Relay reversed horizontal logo" />
            </div>
            <a download="parts-relay-logo-white.svg" href="/assets/logo-white.svg">
              Reversed wordmark <span>SVG ↓</span>
            </a>
          </div>
          <div class="brand-asset">
            <div class="brand-preview">
              <img src="/assets/symbol.svg" alt="Parts Relay symbol" />
            </div>
            <a download="parts-relay-symbol.svg" href="/assets/symbol.svg">
              Primary symbol <span>SVG ↓</span>
            </a>
          </div>
          <div class="brand-asset">
            <div class="brand-preview brand-dark">
              <img src="/assets/symbol-white.svg" alt="Reversed Parts Relay symbol" />
            </div>
            <a download="parts-relay-symbol-white.svg" href="/assets/symbol-white.svg">
              Reversed symbol <span>SVG ↓</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="brand-chapter" id="brand-placement" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>Placing the mark</h2>
        <dl class="brand-guidance">
          <div>
            <dt>Horizontal mark</dt>
            <dd>
              Allow at least 180 pixels of width for the horizontal logo on screen. The SVG already
              includes the margin around the lettering.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Compact spaces</dt>
            <dd>
              The symbol can go as small as 32 pixels wide. Use a favicon in a browser tab and the
              square avatar for a profile picture.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Clear space</dt>
            <dd>
              Use one of the dots in the symbol as your ruler. Leave at least that much space around
              the artwork and resize it in proportion.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Backgrounds</dt>
            <dd>
              On a light background, use the navy and teal logo. On Relay Navy, use the reversed
              file with white lettering and a Mist line. On a photo, find an area where the whole
              line is easy to see.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </section>
      <section class="brand-chapter" id="brand-colors" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>Color</h2>
        <p>
          For a form or reference sheet, set longer instructions in Slate on White or Canvas. Mist
          works well behind a selected item.
        </p>
        <div class="brand-swatches">
          <div class="brand-swatch" style="--swatch: #142b3a">
            <b>Relay Navy</b>
            <span>Identity and headings</span>
            <strong>#142B3A</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="brand-swatch" style="--swatch: #087781">
            <b>Relay Teal</b>
            <span>Actions and emphasis</span>
            <strong>#087781</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="brand-swatch brand-ink" style="--swatch: #dff3ef">
            <b>Mist</b>
            <span>Soft highlights</span>
            <strong>#DFF3EF</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="brand-swatch brand-ink" style="--swatch: #f5f7f8">
            <b>Canvas</b>
            <span>Page backgrounds</span>
            <strong>#F5F7F8</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="brand-swatch" style="--swatch: #455a64">
            <b>Slate</b>
            <span>Body and helper text</span>
            <strong>#455A64</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="brand-swatch brand-ink" style="--swatch: #ffffff">
            <b>White</b>
            <span>Content surfaces</span>
            <strong>#FFFFFF</strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="brand-chapter" id="brand-type" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>Typography</h2>
        <p>
          Use Manrope 600 or 700 for headlines and slide titles. Source Sans 3 comes in 400, 600 and
          700 for body text, field labels, buttons and tables. In email, use Arial or the system
          sans serif.
        </p>
        <div class="brand-spec">
          <div>
            <span>Headings</span>
            <h3 class="brand-manrope">Manrope</h3>
            <p>Front axle assembly</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span>Body text</span>
            <h3 class="brand-source">Source Sans 3</h3>
            <p>Check whether the set includes the wear sensor.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="brand-chapter" id="brand-files" tabindex="-1">
        <h2>Files in the ZIP</h2>
        <dl class="brand-guidance">
          <div>
            <dt>For web and print</dt>
            <dd>
              The wordmarks in the SVG files have outlined lettering. You can send them to a printer
              who doesn’t have Manrope installed.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>For compact layouts</dt>
            <dd>
              The download also contains a stacked logo, a square avatar, and favicons in two sizes
              (32 and 48 pixels).
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>For handoff</dt>
            <dd>
              Designers will find the usage guide and color specifications in the ZIP. Both web
              fonts come with their license notices.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <a
          href="/assets/parts-relay-brand-kit.zip"
          download="Parts-Relay-Brand-Kit.zip"
          class="brand-download"
        >
          Download brand assets ↓
        </a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
